allow a repeat count of zero in artificial arrays

value_repeat rejects a repeat count of less than one:

  (gdb) print array[0]@0
  Invalid number 0 of repetitions.

The count is often a computed value, as in "print *buf@len", and a
length of zero is an ordinary result there.  There is no reason to
refuse it: GDB can represent an empty array, and the previous commit
made the C printer print one as "{}".  Accept zero and reject only
negative counts.

  (gdb) print array[0]@0
  $1 = {}
  (gdb) ptype array[0]@0
  type = int [0]
  (gdb) print array[0]@-1
  Invalid number -1 of repetitions.

